<<^ code="&#x0002;">>

<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Wire — the reified edge

A relation rich enough to //do// something — carry a value, route a message, gate execution, hold a constraint, watch a surface — reifies as its ''own entity'' (has-stack clause 7): a `lar:` addressed record with `from` and `to` fields, wearing its semantics as stack components. The canvas renders wire entities; the messaging plane compiles them; replicas merge them as records.

A wire that merely //points// stays a `loulou`; embedding stays `aka`/`kahea`; composition stays the tags stack. The wire begins where adjacency ends.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ find the relation's real pressure before reifying — value, pulse, message, rule, or watch.
⏿ orient against the ladder: pointer → loulou; embed → aka/kahea; worn → tags; //doing// → wire.
◇ decide the wire's family component and fields; one wire, one arc, one entity.
▶ author the wire record: from, to, worn family, fields as needed; mint missing family memes where pressure warrants.
↺ verify the DAG holds within the family, merge survives concurrent authors, and traces land as their own entities.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/law>>

!! Wire Law

# ''One wire, one entity.'' A wire exists as one `lar:` addressed record carrying `from` and `to` (each a `lar:` URI or `URI#socket`). It MUST NOT exist as an attribute on a line of prose — the corpus-wide attribute-edge form retired 2026-06-12.
# ''Semantics worn, never typed-in-place.'' A wire wears its family as a stack component — `wires/dataflow`, `wires/message`, `wires/control`, `wires/constraint`, `wires/observe` ride as //examples, not an enum// (has-stack clause 4: open minting, ladder-judged). The family definition meme carries the meaning; the wire record carries only endpoints and fields.
# ''The four concerns stay independent'' (inherited whole from the prior edge law): `traversal` (how a query moves) · `propagation` (how invalidation fires) · arity (family-declared, has-stack clause 5) · lifecycle. They ride as ''fields'' on the wire record and MUST NOT collapse into each other.
# ''Lifecycle = template · instance · trace.'' A template wire carries slots and defaults; an instance binds real endpoints; a ''trace'' records a firing, failure, or event — each its own entity, so the event history merges and federates like any record.
# ''Directed, acyclic per family.'' One wire carries one arc. Reciprocal pressure uses two wires. Cycles within a family read as degraded structure.
# ''Wires hold grants.'' As entities, wires wear kapu and capability components like any carrier — a message route can require an operator mint; an attribute on a line never could. Authority = what the wire holds.
# ''The engine vends liveness, wires declare intent.'' A `wires/message` instance compiles into the reaction plane (`ReactionBinding`; engine-vended `listenable`s — `verse-event-lattice` law unchanged). The wire = the authored, addressable declaration; the binding = the engine's live subscription. Events ride wires and lifetime edges — never a global bus.
# ''Canvas renders, never infers.'' The explicit wire entity precedes its spatial form (graph-primacy, `wikispace-canvasspace-ontology`); proximity creates nothing. Wire view-state (path, routing, label placement) lives in view-state entities, never on the wire record.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/authoring>>

!! Authoring — two gestures, one existence (ratified 2026-06-12)

Co-projection applied to wires: the operator's mind originates; the carrier body and the record set both //project// the wire, each in native grain; ''merge authority routes through the CRDT alone''. The dichotomy "text-authored sigils vs reified entities" dissolves — both hold, at different grains:

| grain | a wire appears as | authority | gesture |
|---|---|---|---|
| disk carrier | body pranala sigil (memory-palace form) | projection only | text editing |
| CRDT records | the wire entity | ''merge authority'' | the compile target |
| canvas | rendered wire + drag-authoring | view; writes records | direct manipulation |
| runtime | engine-vended `ReactionBinding` | ephemeral | compiled from records |

# ''The text authors; the record exists; the CRDT merges.'' A body sigil MUST NOT carry runtime authority — the same boundary Verse itself draws between source text and scene entities.
# ''Deterministic identity.'' A body-authored wire derives its address as `<parent-uri>/wires/<anchor>` — the `#anchor` names the wire; re-ingest converges (normalize-once). A sigil without an anchor never compiles; `loulou` stays adjacency forever.
# ''Hierarchy = lifetime, applied.'' A body-authored wire lives as its carrier's child: dies with it, projects back into that carrier's file alone (projection follows lifetime; a wire never re-renders into a body it did not originate from). Cross-carrier wires owned by neither endpoint get authored as their own entities — the canvas gesture's native case.
# ''Declared-unresolved wires read fertile.'' A body pranala whose wire entity has not yet materialized stands as a lawful placeholder — the memory-palace form — awaiting the compiler, exactly as a bare tag awaits its definition.
# ''The compiler rides INGEST.'' Body-sigil → wire-record compilation shares the shore's organs (replace-by-group apply, three-way diff, echo-proof round-trip) and SHALL ride that vector, never precede it. `edgesFromMemeAst` already walks sigils into flat edge records — the compiler's front half, standing.

<<~/ahu>>

